{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1357090-are-aberrants-actually-novas","id":1357090,"title":"Are Aberrants actually Novas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-26T13:07:26-08:00","id":1357090,"title":"Are Aberrants actually Novas?","content":"After reading the section on Aberrants in TC:Aeon and the Aberrant manuscript, my slowly forming headcannon is that Aberrants are, in fact, a separate species or a mutation of Nova, not the same thing. Their inherent, well, corruption seems fully ingrained in their being - almost no Aberrant is sane or even vaguely human, while many Novas, including those on Eden, and Divis Mal (at least as of the 2060s), and Caestus Pax (who has 40+ years of Quantum power) have remained relative stability.<br /> <br /> Perhaps any Nova COULD become an Aberrant, but really, most are more likely to obtain complete Transcendence than to reach such heights of mutation and not do so. The fact that there are Novas remaining that are not referred to as Aberrants (Edenites, and for a time those in Nippon), as well as them having slightly different abilities - it appears Aberrants, for example, can be telepathic but are far less likely to be a mega-genius), I think supports this as well. Maybe more than one mutation occurred in humans that enabled them to access Quantum powers. Maybe the rise of Quantum usage from Novas led to the creation of Aberrants.<br /> <br /> Surely someone in the Aeon Trinity has a similar theory in universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T14:48:06-08:00","id":1357117,"title":"","content":"There are some Novas that have a \u201cknack\u201d for corruption, but it\u2019s not a separate idea. <br /> <br /> There are a few explanations on the reason why Mal and Pax didn\u2019t raise corruption.<br /> <br /> The first is They did, but focused on mental transformations. The fact Mal had already 4 Chrisalys by the beginning of Aberrant.<br /> <br /> The second is before N-Day, novas we\u2019re not as powerful as hey were after but they were not as prone to corruption too.<br /> <br /> The third is the more novas around more corruption is generated. Basically they are radioactive, but the environment \u201cdigest\u201d this radiation slowly to the point no corruption is accumulated. If there are too many novas the environment would not be capable and the corruption would raise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T15:08:59-08:00","id":1357121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1357090-are-aberrants-actually-novas?p=1357117#post1357117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third is the more novas around more corruption is generated. Basically they are radioactive, but the environment \u201cdigest\u201d this radiation slowly to the point no corruption is accumulated. If there are too many novas the environment would not be capable and the corruption would raise.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the rules don't fully support this reading, it is how the setting comes across to me, with the caveat that some Novas are much, much more radioactive than others. All it takes is one Nova who spews flux around everywhere to start a horrific chain reaction, where newly erupted Novas start out with high levels of Transcendence, and automatically start pumping out even more flux, creating entire generations of Aberrant Novas.<br /> <br /> There are several pieces of corroborating evidence in the text. Those few Novas still erupting on Earth mostly seem to come from Corruption zones, and so seem to erupt with abnormally high Transcendence. The Eden Novas are all fine despite having high Quantum, presumably because the planet didn't have any Aberrants there spewing flux all over everything. Many of the Aberrant Novas who attacked Australia weren't Aberrant until a high Transcendence Aberrant corrupted them with flux powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T17:17:48-08:00","id":1357136,"title":"","content":"Figure most of the Aberrants in the Aeon book are generally &quot;sub-aberrants&quot; - humans mutated via Flux into twisted abominations. Actual Transcendent Novas are pretty rare on Earth. But those that do erupt on Earth tend to be corrupted because the main source of Quantum is in the corrupted zones. Somebody not in those zones will probably manifest as a latent psion because overall there's a lot more sub-quantum energy on Earth than quantum energy.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T12:32:04-08:00","id":1357234,"title":"","content":"The large sidebar bordering on full page spread on page 192 of \u00c6on talks about how some Aberrants suffer from a form of instability that generates additional Corruption, and that Corruption begets more corruption.<br /> <br /> In the Aberrant manuscript there is a high level transformation that causes you to emit Flux that even affects Baselines, and gives them Transformations as if it were Transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T13:34:12-08:00","id":1357247,"title":"","content":"There are a few other things, first most of the Novas that left Earth didn\u2019t return and are still around exploring or colonizing other planets. The ones that are back are the most crazy, violent and vengeful ones, it means they are probably the most transcendent ones (probably).<br /> <br /> The thing about the Sub-Aberrant mutants is very important too, in Aberrant terms, they are not Novas, they are mutated baselines, only got powers from transformations and not from proper quantum use. In this end the Aberrants we battle more often in Aeon are truly another species and not Novas, but it\u2019s not what OP really meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T14:02:49-08:00","id":1357599,"title":"","content":"Also, if you hit Quantum 10 without hitting Transcendence 10, you're... just no longer <i>here</i>. It's very much a Childhood's end scenario, so whether they were hostile or frendly to baselines, the destinies have been forever sundered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}